  "notes": "ぱさぱさ is an onomatopoeia/mimetic word describing dry, rough, crumbly texture.\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- ぱさぱさだ: is dry (na-adjective)\n- ぱさぱさ⟦している→する：00392_suru⟧: is dry (verb form)\n- ぱさぱさ⟦に→に：00314_ni⟧⟦なる→なる：01970_naru⟧: to become dry\n\nCOMMONLY DESCRIBES:\n- ⟦{髪|かみ}→髪：02196_kami⟧: dry hair\n- ⟦{肌|はだ}→肌：02243_hada⟧: dry skin\n- ⟦パン→パン：00553_pan⟧: dry, crumbly bread\n- ⟦ケーキ→ケーキ：01356_keeki⟧: dry cake\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- ぱさぱさ: dry, lacking moisture\n- ⟦しっとり→しっとり：05837_shittori⟧: moist, supple\n- ⟦ふわふわ→ふわふわ：05156_fuwafuwa⟧: fluffy, soft\n- ⟦さらさら→さらさら：05255_sarasara⟧: smooth, silky (for hair)\n\nUSAGE:\nThe voiced version ⟦ばさばさ→ばさばさ：noentry⟧ describes rustling sounds or rough/disheveled appearance.",
